<Layouts.app flash={@flash} current_scope={assigns[:current_scope]}>
  <section
    id="landing-hero"
    class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-10 px-4 py-14 sm:px-6 lg:grid-cols-[1.05fr_0.95fr] lg:py-24"
  >
    <div class="flex flex-col justify-center">
      <p class="ta-eyebrow">For Cameroon secondary teachers · APC / CBA</p>
      <h1 class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-4xl font-bold leading-[1.05] tracking-tight text-base-content sm:text-6xl">
        Teach the whole programme. <span class="ta-mark">Know it</span> at a glance.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-xl text-lg leading-8 text-base-content/75">
        Every term starts with a <em>fiche de progression</em>
        shared as a PDF in a WhatsApp group —
        and ends with no one quite sure how much of the syllabus was actually covered. Teacher
        Assistant turns that plan into a living tracker: build it once, tick off what you teach each
        week, and watch your <em>taux de couverture</em>
        climb. On your phone, in French or English.
      </p>

      <div id="home-actions" class="mt-8 flex flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row">
        <.link navigate={~p"/register"} class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">
          <.icon name="hero-academic-cap" class="size-5" /> Create your free account
        </.link>
        <.link navigate={~p"/sign-in"} class="btn btn-outline btn-lg">
          <.icon name="hero-arrow-left-on-rectangle" class="size-5" /> Sign in
        </.link>
      </div>

      <dl class="mt-10 grid max-w-md grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <div>
          <dt class="ta-num text-2xl font-semibold text-base-content">6</dt>
          <dd class="text-xs text-base-content/60">administrative sequences</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="ta-num text-2xl font-semibold text-base-content">36</dt>
          <dd class="text-xs text-base-content/60">weeks tracked</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="ta-num text-2xl font-semibold text-base-content">FR·EN</dt>
          <dd class="text-xs text-base-content/60">both subsystems</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class="ta-board flex flex-col gap-5 self-center p-6 sm:p-7">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4">
        <div>
          <p class="ta-eyebrow">Taux de couverture</p>
          <p class="font-display text-lg font-semibold">This year, so far</p>
        </div>
        <span class="ta-num rounded-full border border-base-300 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-base-content/70">
          Week 6 · Seq 2
        </span>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-4">
        <div>
          <div class="mb-1.5 text-sm font-semibold">Mathématiques · 6e A</div>
          <.coverage_ribbon rate={62} />
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="mb-1.5 text-sm font-semibold">Français · 5e B</div>
          <.coverage_ribbon rate={48} behind?={true} />
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="mb-1.5 text-sm font-semibold">SVT · 4e A</div>
          <.coverage_ribbon rate={81} />
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="text-xs leading-5 text-base-content/60">
        Each track is split into the six sequences of the school year. Green is on pace; yellow is
        falling behind.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="landing-reality" class="border-y border-base-300 bg-base-100">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6">
      <p class="ta-eyebrow">The reality today</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-2xl font-bold leading-snug sm:text-3xl">
        The plan lives in a PDF, coverage is a guess, and the scramble always comes in June.
      </h2>
      <div class="mt-8 grid gap-6 text-sm leading-6 text-base-content/75 sm:grid-cols-3">
        <p>
          You teach across one or more schools, juggling several subject–class pairs — and the only
          record of the plan is a screenshot in a chat.
        </p>
        <p>
          Mid-year, “Where are we in the programme?” has no honest answer until someone counts back
          through the cahier de textes by hand.
        </p>
        <p>
          By the third term, the gap between what was planned and what was taught is a surprise — at
          exactly the wrong moment.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="product-proof" class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
    <p class="ta-eyebrow">The weekly loop</p>
    <h2 class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-2xl font-bold sm:text-3xl">
      Built around the school year — not another spreadsheet to reconcile at term's end.
    </h2>

    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="ta-leaf">
        <span class="ta-num text-sm font-semibold text-primary">01</span>
        <h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-lg font-semibold">Build the fiche</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-base-content/75">
          Lay out modules and lessons across the six sequences — planned hours, lesson type, and
          optional competence-based fields. Reuse a plan to set up the next class in minutes.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="ta-leaf">
        <span class="ta-num text-sm font-semibold text-primary">02</span>
        <h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-lg font-semibold">Log what you taught</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-base-content/75">
          A few taps after class: pick the lesson, mark it done or partial, record the hours. Your <em>cahier de textes</em>, kept current without the paperwork.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="ta-leaf">
        <span class="ta-num text-sm font-semibold text-primary">03</span>
        <h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-lg font-semibold">Watch the coverage</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-base-content/75">
          Your <em>taux de couverture</em> per subject and sequence — always honest about what was
          planned versus what was actually taught. No more June surprises.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="landing-features" class="border-y border-base-300 bg-base-100">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-8 px-4 py-14 sm:px-6 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
        <span class="grid size-10 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-lg bg-primary/15 text-primary">
          <.icon name="hero-device-phone-mobile" class="size-5" />
        </span>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold">Made for your phone</h3>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-6 text-base-content/70">
            Quick, forgiving interactions built for a smartphone on a patchy connection — your work
            is never lost to a dropped request.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
        <span class="grid size-10 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-lg bg-primary/15 text-primary">
          <.icon name="hero-language" class="size-5" />
        </span>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold">Bilingual by design</h3>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-6 text-base-content/70">
            Francophone and Anglophone subsystems, French or English interface — switch any time.
            Built for one national system, two tracks.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
        <span class="grid size-10 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-lg bg-primary/15 text-primary">
          <.icon name="hero-lock-closed" class="size-5" />
        </span>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold">Yours, and private</h3>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-6 text-base-content/70">
            Your personal workspace belongs to you alone — no school required. School workspaces
            build on the same foundation, later.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
        <span class="grid size-10 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-lg bg-primary/15 text-primary">
          <.icon name="hero-academic-cap" class="size-5" />
        </span>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold">Grounded in real practice</h3>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-6 text-base-content/70">
            Six sequences, 36 weeks, integration weeks, APC fields — modeled on how Cameroonian
            schools actually run, not a generic template.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="workflow-index" class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
    <div class="ta-board flex flex-col items-center gap-5 px-6 py-12 text-center sm:px-8">
      <p class="ta-eyebrow">Start free, in one sitting</p>
      <h2 class="max-w-2xl text-2xl font-bold sm:text-3xl">
        Set up your first fiche de progression today — on the bus home, if you like.
      </h2>
      <p class="max-w-xl text-sm leading-6 text-base-content/70">
        Sign up free and you'll have an active plan and your first coverage reading before the kettle
        boils. School tools — roll call, report cards, fees — build on the same desk later.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-2 flex flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row">
        <.link navigate={~p"/register"} class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">
          <.icon name="hero-academic-cap" class="size-5" /> Create your free account
        </.link>
        <.link navigate={~p"/teacher"} class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg">
          Open teacher desk <.icon name="hero-arrow-right" class="size-4" />
        </.link>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layouts.app>
